# Cases for core-language-docs/sets.md. Read by ../run-all.sh, which
# discovers every */CASES under snippets/ rather than carrying a list.
#
# Five pipe-separated fields:
#
#   module | cfg | expected-rc | distinct-states | what it shows
#
# A blank line or a line opening with # is skipped.
#
# THE FOURTH FIELD IS THE STATE COUNT, and on this page it carries more of the
# argument than the rc does. Set cardinality IS the state space here, so three
# of the page's findings are counts over runs that all exit 0:
#
#   Quarry 3 against QuarryPick 1   drawing from a set against CHOOSE
#   Silos 16                        the reachable states ARE the powerset
#   Caliper 0                       an empty interval, checked over nothing
#
# Caliper is the one to protect. It exits 0 and prints "No error has been
# found" over an invariant no state can satisfy, because there are no states.
# An rc-only suite would call that a pass. Leave the field empty where the
# page quotes no count.
#
# Exit codes TLC uses here:
#   0    all checks passed, which includes passing over zero states
#   12   an invariant was violated by a state
#   150  parse or semantic error in the module
#   151  a declared invariant evaluated to FALSE with no state involved

